input_prompt: Explain what on-device AI means in simple terms.
INFO: Loaded OpenCL library with dlopen.


On-device AI is like having a smart computer that can think and make decisions right on your phone, tablet, or computer, without needing to connect to the internet or a server. It’s like having a tiny brain in your device that can process information and learn from it, all while keeping your data private and your device faster. For example, if you take a photo, your phone’s camera might use on-device AI to recognize what’s in the picture instantly, without waiting for the data to go back to the cloud. This makes it quicker and more secure than relying on cloud services.

